      "description": "Your Mac. A whole new way to carry it.\n\nPocket Mac Lab brings your own Mac desktop and sound to iPhone, iPad and iPhone Duo. Use touch, an on-screen keyboard, a spacious trackpad or your own compatible keyboard and mouse.\n\nYOUR DESKTOP, WHEREVER YOU ARE\nPair with your Mac, then reconnect from home or another network. Your Mac must stay awake, online, signed in and running Pocket Mac Connector. After restarting the Mac, local sign-in may be needed before remote access is available.\n\nMADE FOR YOUR DEVICE\nOn iPhone and iPad, use a clear desktop view with a separate trackpad and left/right click controls. Rotate to portrait for a display above your keyboard or trackpad. Open the movable floating keyboard without changing your full-screen desktop.\n\nROOM TO MOVE\nPoint, click, drag and scroll. An optional ridged scroll wheel gives you a dedicated scrolling surface. Pinch where you want to zoom, pan with two fingers and let the view follow your pointer near the edges. Fit whole Mac restores the complete desktop. Switch between detected Mac monitors with the display selector.\n\nBRING YOUR OWN SETUP\nConnect a compatible Bluetooth or USB keyboard and mouse to your device. Type, use shortcuts, click, drag and scroll. Mac audio plays on your device when enabled. Mac controls and monitor switching require the companion permissions shown during setup.\n\nA LITTLE LAPTOP ON IPHONE DUO\nChoose Studio Silver, Studio Space Black, Daybreak, Circuit, Midnight, Tide, Ember or Slate. The themed keyboard and matching pear cover follow your choice. Fold into a laptop, open fully or close to show your cover. Themes and covers are exclusive to iPhone Duo.\n\nA LITTLE DESKTOP, BUILT IN\nExplore the local launcher, gallery, calculator, games and Photo Room without a Mac. These mini apps do not run macOS; your connected Mac provides the real desktop. Photo Room includes a nine-filter grid and saves pictures to the in-app gallery.\n\nPRIVATE PAIRING\nFirst connection uses your Mac account login plus matching-code approval on your Mac. Approved devices can reconnect without scanning again. Optional remembered passwords stay in device-only Keychain. Forget the saved Mac or revoke sharing from the companion whenever needed.\n\nGETTING CONNECTED\nAirDrop the free signed and notarized Mac companion from the app. Drag it into Applications and follow its guided setup for Screen Sharing, Screen & System Audio Recording and Accessibility. A compatible Mac running macOS 15 or later and working internet on both devices are required. Performance depends on your devices and networks.\n\nPaid upfront. No subscriptions or in-app purchases. Independent; not affiliated with or endorsed by Apple.\n\nSupport: https://pocket-mac-declann.declann-tan-9532.chatgpt.site/support.html\nPrivacy Policy: https://pocket-mac-declann.declann-tan-9532.chatgpt.site/privacy.html\nTerms of Use: https://www.apple.com/legal/internet-services/itunes/dev/stdeula/",
